# What is generated, and what is deliberately absent.
#
# out/ holds takes and renders -- large, stamped, and reproducible from the
# scripts. footage/ is the opposite: two and a half seconds of a real phone
# scanning a real identity card, which nothing here can regenerate, so it is
# tracked.
#
# soundtrack.mp3 is optional: assemble.sh uses it if it is there and builds a
# silent video if it is not. soundtrack.json says which track the prototypes
# were cut against.
#
# fonts/ and package-lock.json used to be ignored. They are pinned now: the
# faces are OFL and the pipeline will not render a card without them, and a
# floating Playwright is a video that stops building six months from now.
node_modules/
out/
!footage/
tapfx/
espeak/
tts-venv/
voices/
casting/
vo_parts/
video*/
*.png
soundtrack.mp3
